# firewall pve-states ------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Mock: Proxmox VE's screen where it says less than the two$
# hosts: pve-firewall stopped, sshd on another port, a$
# blacklist, and a node where origin/main left ufw active, which$
# nothing here shows (decision 7).$
$
# pve-firewall stopped -----------------------------------------$
$
# Firewall Configuration #######################################$
$
  [?] Firewall             Unknown pve-firewall stopped$
$
# pve-firewall -------------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Service              Stopped$
   -  Enabled              Yes$
   -  Incoming policy      Drop$
  [?] SSH (22)             Unknown$
  [?] Web UI (8006)        Unknown$
   -  hardn reads pve-firewall and doesn't change it: a wrong$
      rule can cut off the web UI and the cluster.$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0 or q]:$
$
# sshd on 2230 -------------------------------------------------$
$
# Firewall Configuration #######################################$
$
  [?] Firewall             Unknown 2230 may be blocked$
$
# pve-firewall -------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Service              Running$
  [+] Enabled              Yes$
  [+] Incoming policy      Drop$
  [ ] SSH (22)             Management network sshd on 2230$
  [+] Web UI (8006)        Management network$
   -  hardn reads pve-firewall and doesn't change it: a wrong$
      rule can cut off the web UI and the cluster.$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0 or q]:$
$
# a blacklist --------------------------------------------------$
$
# Firewall Configuration #######################################$
$
  [?] Firewall             Unknown ssh may be blocked$
$
# pve-firewall -------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Service              Running$
  [+] Enabled              Yes$
  [+] Incoming policy      Drop$
  [?] SSH (22)             Unknown$
  [?] Web UI (8006)        Unknown$
  [ ] Blacklist            Has entries$
   -  hardn reads pve-firewall and doesn't change it: a wrong$
      rule can cut off the web UI and the cluster.$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0 or q]:$
$
# ufw left active by origin/main -------------------------------$
$
# Firewall Configuration #######################################$
$
  [ ] Firewall             Not Configured disabled$
$
# pve-firewall -------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Service              Running$
  [ ] Enabled              No$
   -  Incoming policy      Drop$
   -  SSH (22)             Not filtered$
   -  Web UI (8006)        Not filtered$
   -  hardn reads pve-firewall and doesn't change it: a wrong$
      rule can cut off the web UI and the cluster.$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0 or q]:$
$
$

